# Line endings are a correctness property here, not a preference.
#
# Without this file a Windows checkout rewrites every text file to CRLF, which
# silently breaks two things this repository depends on:
#
#   * A shebang becomes "#!/usr/bin/env node\r". Unix resolves that as an
#     interpreter literally named "node\r", so every bin script and every
#     documented `node scripts/src/e2e.mjs` invocation fails on macOS and
#     Linux with "no such file or directory". release-packaging.test.mjs
#     asserts the first line byte for byte.
#   * Line-ending sensitive assertions break against checked-out files, which
#     is how apps/desktop/release.test.mjs came to read Cargo.lock with a
#     pattern that only matches LF.
#
# Text is LF in the repository and LF in the working tree. Windows editors and
# tools that need CRLF are configured per file type further down.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonc text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.rs    text eol=lf
*.swift text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.lock  text eol=lf
Cargo.lock text eol=lf
pnpm-lock.yaml text eol=lf

